request: Items with due dates sort before items without.

single call 0: edit -> src/commands.ts, src/commands.test.ts  (Items with due dates now sort before items without in `list`: after the includeDone filter, the visible todos are copied and sorted with a `hasDue(b) - hasDue(a)` comparator, so dated items come first while Array.prototype.sort's stability preserves the existing relative order in each group. Since `run`'s list case delegates to `list`, the CLI output is sorted too, and `format` stays a pure renderer. Added a test in commands.test.ts covering the new ordering (dated item listed before two undated items, whose relative order is kept); existing tests are untouched and still pass because undated-only lists are unaffected by the stable sort.)
round 1: oracle GREEN
single call 1: accept  (Items with due dates now sort before items without: `list` sorts the visible todos (after the includeDone filter) with a `hasDue(b) - hasDue(a)` comparator, whose stability preserves relative order within each group, and the CLI `run` list path inherits this via `list`. A new test in commands.test.ts asserts a dated item is listed before undated items while their relative order is kept; tsc --noEmit and all 11 vitest tests pass.)

